{"reviews":[{"id":"arka-v3-train-prompt-0303","row_sha256":"416375366a1f1ff4bad6095ce4aa380abcd3f3c7c097b38473382bcf82d024aa","critique":"The output keeps every note: the clip-on install, live whole-home use, 30 days of hourly storage, the lag caveat and the ban on claiming appliance identification. Sam's quote is reproduced verbatim, lowercase included, and the output restructures the request without performing it.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-prompt-0305","row_sha256":"7724487d6e06c6026acc96543aa124db402292aac4adedd7c1f79f0d1212a34e","critique":"Changing 'material i pasted' to 'supplied material' is a faithful rewording. The focus on usage and costs and the brevity constraint are both preserved, and nothing is invented.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-prompt-0304","row_sha256":"6a09600f9c7c97c66c45b313651def285de10b108786eeeb9c8f24c0f064f9e8","critique":"The German prompt keeps the simple guide, the evening and night readings, the instruction to explain only which values to compare, and the ban on product suggestions. Orthography is improved and no content is lost.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-prompt-0289","row_sha256":"18e9dca0e6214691b19e5e5f85f1902a63d5be3ba4c55e3334f1364d64565578","critique":"The output is well organized, but it drops several supplied constraints and hedges. Specific defects:
- The request 'please don't assume it will come out with one particular treatment' for the cloudy patch is omitted.
- The explicit 'i don't want a plan that starts by hauling it outside' is omitted.
- The hedge 'i can't say whether she meant that the original finish must stay untouched' is dropped.
- 'two of the drawer pulls have loose screws' becomes 'two drawer-pull screws are loose', which changes the quantity.
- The user's openness to cleaning and small repairs, and possibly refinishing the top, is reduced to a negative framing.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"fail","verdict":"fail"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-prompt-0307","row_sha256":"8ebaa73b2ad861d8c42ea332a3f30e30c07e0ae380902c51672f48031caaf9c5","critique":"This is an identity row, and the output is byte-identical to the already well-formed input request.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-prompt-0311","row_sha256":"c44cd73b3b97a494ccd3b538886b56ffbf613fa8576cbfcaba1007404200a90c","critique":"The short-paragraph limit, the focus on orders and delivery timing, and the 'use only the notes' constraint are all preserved. Rendering 'i'll paste them next' as 'notes I provide' is acceptable.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-prompt-0306","row_sha256":"682f793242ecbeec29323a5d84139980a02ed99d6954c27c256d7e83a2535085","critique":"The output is a usable prompt that preserves all of the following:
- the mixed audience of past users and non-users;
- the three focus areas;
- the difficulties and pre-purchase questions;
- the exclusion of energy policy;
- the no-presentation and no-product-explanation constraints;
- the instruction not to answer the questions.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-prompt-0312","row_sha256":"b9a829edf05093457c8efbcea9fa47716ba96bc5fd8e485d270a9241cc6277b9","critique":"The final question 'what's the biggest thing that makes a delivery feel worth it?' is reworded to 'What do you think makes a delivery feel worth it?', which drops 'the biggest thing'. It is also recast as a direct question to the model, inviting an answer, rather than kept as a discussion question or clarified. The output also weakens the input's tentative 'maybe include cost and delivery times' into a firm requirement.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"fail","verdict":"fail"}]}
